title: Summary timeout causal recovery
status: source verified; live recovery not yet verified
observations:
  - Celly instance 9385-52ea0f8a2296 logged identity admission pause after restart.
  - Last activity 2026-10-22T12:46:50 failed at 3/31 chunks, 4 calls, RuntimeError.
  - Two fourth summary calls ended at the 120 second timeout.
changes:
  - Recognize explicit transport exceptions through RuntimeError cause chains.
  - Retry only failed internal tool-free map summaries, at most three attempts.
  - Retain completed summaries in the current run and honor cancellation and deadline.
  - Exhausted retries propagate failure, never substitute a truncated source excerpt.
limits:
  - Does not prove tokenizer accuracy or explain the initial oversized conversation.
  - Completed summaries are not persisted across process restarts.
  - Does not claim successful recovery of the live Celly checkpoint.
validation:
  - 39 compaction tests pass, including real loopback HTTP timeout and recovery.
  - Runtime group: 441 tests pass, 19 skipped.
  - Ruff and project documentation metadata checks pass.
initial_failure_correlation:
  - Native compaction started at 02:27:50 local, before the 02:29:36 visible prompt-too-long error.
  - At 02:27:50, 02:28:22, and 02:28:49 external injection logged deferred native_compaction.
  - After failures, deferred context_recovery records remained present.
  - No channel_stdin_proxy_injected record appears in the inspected 02:15 through 02:30 interval.
  - Therefore this initial interval does not support continuous external-message injection as the demonstrated cause.
  - At 07:29:20 UTC DeepSeek reported total input 700835; at 07:29:36 UTC Claude reported 935102.
  - Provider-switch usage differs materially; the exact request payload and tokenizer counts must be compared before attributing causation.
installed_validation:
  - Six transport recovery tests were executed against the installed local-share module and passed.
  - npm publication run 39838396344 completed successfully.
